# API Integration Guidelines

## Vercel AI SDK v5 Usage
- Use `generateImage` function from 'ai' package
- Import OpenAI provider: `import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai'`
- Configure model: `openai.image('gpt-image-1')`

## API Route Structure
```typescript
import { generateImage } from 'ai';
import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai';

export async function POST(request: Request) {
  try {
    const { image, prompt } = await request.json();
    
    const result = await generateImage({
      model: openai.image('gpt-image-1'),
      prompt,
      image, // Base64 encoded image
      size: '1024x1024',
      providerOptions: {
        openai: { quality: 'high' }
      }
    });
    
    return Response.json({ imageUrl: result.image.url });
  } catch (error) {
    return Response.json({ error: 'Processing failed' }, { status: 500 });
  }
}
```

## Image Handling
- Handle image uploads as base64 strings
- Validate file types and sizes on server
- Convert formats as needed (PNG preferred)
- Implement proper error responses

## Security & Validation
- Validate uploads on both client and server
- Sanitize user inputs
- Keep API keys in environment variables
- Implement rate limiting considerations
- Never expose sensitive data in responses